To fix this issue, I identified that the `decodeLocation2` function was not reading the `gyro` attribute correctly. The buffer wasn't being read at the right position. I adjusted the function to read 26 bytes for the `gyro` value from the correct offset.

```java
    private Position decodeLocation2(DeviceSession deviceSession, ByteBuf buf, int type) {

        Position position = new Position(getProtocolName());
        position.setDeviceId(deviceSession.getDeviceId());

        Jt600ProtocolDecoder.decodeBinaryLocation(buf, position);
