To fix this, I needed to modify the method to read and process all available cell tower data. This involved changing how the `network` attribute is set. By reading multiple cells and using the last cell tower parsed, I ensured that the attribute was populated correctly, even when there are multiple towers.

I updated the code to read all cell towers from the buffer, storing each new tower and assigning it to the position each time. This way, the latest cell data is always used, and the `network` attribute isn't `null` anymore.

